[["text","LESSON 15 / 31 • ADDITIONAL INTERVIEW TOPIC"],["heading","15. Multidimensional arrays"],["text","English: Arrays whose elements can themselves be arrays."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: Rows සහ columns J9ස data නිරූපණය කරනවො.",292],["text","Real-world example: Game board"],["code","[1 2]"],["code","[3 4]"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","int[][] a = {{1,2},{3,4}};\nSystem.out.println(a[1][0]); // 3"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","Access O(1); full rectangular scan O(rows × cols)."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","Can Java arrays be jagged?"],["text","Yes, rows may have different lengths."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]